# Ansible Learning Lab

This repository contains my Ansible practice playbooks, inventory files, and automation examples for Linux server administration and DevOps tasks.

## Overview

The purpose of this repository is to learn and practice:

* Ansible Inventory Management
* Ad-hoc Commands
* Playbook Development
* Package Installation
* Service Management
* File Transfer Automation
* Linux Administration
* Infrastructure Automation

## Repository Structure

```text
ansible/
├── inventory
├── playbook.yml
├── copy_zip.yml
└── README.md
```

## Inventory

The inventory file contains the target hosts managed by Ansible.

Example:

```ini
[web]
<server-ip>

[web:vars]
ansible_user=ubuntu
ansible_ssh_private_key_file=/path/to/key.pem
```

## Sample Playbooks

### Install Nginx and Docker

This playbook performs:

* Update package cache
* Install Nginx
* Start and enable Nginx
* Install Docker
* Start and enable Docker

Run:

```bash
ansible-playbook -i inventory playbook.yml
```

### Copy ZIP File to Remote Server

This playbook copies a ZIP file from the Ansible control node to the target server.

Run:

```bash
ansible-playbook -i inventory copy_zip.yml
```

## Useful Commands

### Test Connectivity

```bash
ansible all -i inventory -m ping
```

### Gather Facts

```bash
ansible all -i inventory -m setup
```

### Check Service Status

```bash
ansible web -i inventory -m shell -a "systemctl status nginx --no-pager"
```

### Run a Playbook

```bash
ansible-playbook -i inventory playbook.yml
```

## Technologies Used

* Ansible
* Linux
* Ubuntu
* AWS EC2
* SSH
* YAML

## Learning Objectives

* Automate repetitive Linux administration tasks
* Manage multiple servers from a central control node
* Deploy and configure applications consistently
* Improve infrastructure management using Infrastructure as Code (IaC)